  "body": "Stacked on REC PR #94 (`8071d2e26d1befe2efe4599c5abd416d90e5e031`); **draft, no merge/adoption**.\n\n### This unit (real code + executions)\n- Self-contained, source-faithful **short FLRW q=0 hydrogen-only** controlled history experiment: two real + 311 algebraic virtual levels via original HyRec2012 full atomic source, accepted-only causal photon histories, preallocated column-major outgoing history, explicit positive-gated chemistry and implicit positive Compton thermal step. Uses *synthetic zero photon prehistory*, deliberately **not** a primordial HyRec FULL solved historical (x_e(z)).\n- New read-only REC PR94 donor -> REI PR150 config gate, pinned PR150 Git blob `d9dcdbb4b33ebfe89f6c1322cba2a83a7bab15a6`; catches IC drift, nonzero q, wrong epoch and unauthorized activation. It never mutates REI.\n- Actual Wolfram Engine 15 + xAct xTensor1.3.0 executed 5 checks for metric compatibility and Bianchi-I Killing energy/volume, with archived script and output. No claim that this establishes an Einstein-dynamical high-z Bianchi background.\n- Fresh local Ubuntu suite **484 PASS / 41 deselected**, unmodified original HyRec C source parity targeted slow **1 PASS**, focused tests **16 PASS**. Code compileall PASS and staged diff whitespace check PASS.\n- Controlled 3-grid refinement with differences decreasing: x_HII successive differences 1.00964e-5 -> 3.19689e-6, Tm 0.11358 -> 0.04874 K. Four independent 45-step cases threaded2 were **slower** (measured serial/parallel median 0.8186); do not claim 64-way speedup.\n\n### Explicit science gate / REI boundary\n- Original HyRec FULL H+He z20 donor remains opt-in disabled: x_HII=0.000210349192936, Tgas=9.306042400380866 K, zero ionizing stock; REI original source scenario SHA `07aa11d2d3fd47d2ed95e9d9161f6205e4d9ba386c27ad43d2b298fcd86d1696`.\n- **NOT RUN**: REI native sensitivity experiment, proper C-matched accepted FULL primordial H-only integration across its complete range, high-z self-consistent signed Bianchi recombination, any CMB observables. New short synthetic q0 track is **not** transferred as REI donor.\n- NCP 64CPU/128GiB production workload not launched; this unit needed only bounded lightweight local tests. REI native production is separately controlled by PR150.\n- Report, verification receipts, three-grid/n-thread numeric JSON, xAct WL+output, typed cross-repo contract, testable code in `research/rec_r3d_full_short_20261015/`.\n\n### Stop condition / next\nDo not merge before independent original-C accepted-history comparison with actual physical initial photon prehistory and long-horizon convergence. Native REI conditional source runs require fresh q0 initial state and native charge/energy/opacity ledgers with separate positive transport grid-refinement gates, never old checkpoint resume.",
